  "environment_bible": "Use abstract, nearly empty environments made from off-white paper fields, charcoal ground shadows, rough ink edges, and broad open thresholds. Rooms should remain symbolic rather than literal: no desks, phones, notebooks, calendars, bedrooms, offices, signs, screens, or explanatory objects. Doors and passages may be wide open, sealed, distorted, or missing their keyholes, but they must read as psychological boundaries rather than architectural locations. The old key is the recurring object and the only controlled gold element; all other objects remain black, charcoal, or off-white. Black ink bands can emerge from the key and wrap around wrists to represent a former protective response becoming restrictive, then gradually loosen as awareness develops. Use sparse background silhouettes or shadow traces to suggest former environmental pressure without depicting a crowd. Maintain generous negative space, soft charcoal transitions, and clear focal hierarchy. All generated visuals remain text-free, with no visible writing in any language.",
